WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.697 --> 00:01.698 align:center line:81%
Thank you, choir.

00:03.300 --> 00:04.301 align:center line:81%
Thank you,

00:05.068 --> 00:06.370 align:center line:81%
President Oaks.

00:07.738 --> 00:09.473 align:center line:81%
We love and sustain you,

00:10.440 --> 00:15.112 align:center line:79%
and we join you in your heartfelt
expressions of love

00:15.112 --> 00:20.450 align:center line:79%
and admiration for our dear President
Russell M. Nelson and his family.

00:22.953 --> 00:25.489 align:center line:81%
Last year, during a trip to Europe,

00:26.723 --> 00:29.326 align:center line:81%
I visited my old place of employment,

00:29.326 --> 00:32.329 align:center line:79%
Lufthansa German Airlines,
at the Frankfurt Airport.

00:33.964 --> 00:35.165 align:center line:81%
To train its pilots,

00:35.165 --> 00:39.670 align:center line:79%
they operate several sophisticated
full-motion flight simulators

00:40.170 --> 00:44.508 align:center line:79%
that can recreate almost any normal
and emergency flight condition.

00:44.775 --> 00:46.977 align:center line:79%
During my many years
as an airline captain,

00:46.977 --> 00:48.512 align:center line:81%
I had to pass a check flight

00:48.579 --> 00:54.084 align:center line:79%
in the flight simulator every six
months to keep my pilot license current.

00:54.651 --> 01:00.324 align:center line:79%
I remember well those intense moments
of stress and anxiety,

01:01.124 --> 01:06.430 align:center line:79%
but also the feeling of accomplishment
after passing the test.

01:07.164 --> 01:10.300 align:center line:79%
Back then, I was young
and loved the challenge.

01:10.467 --> 01:14.905 align:center line:79%
During my visit, one of the Lufthansa
executives asked if I would like

01:15.238 --> 01:19.509 align:center line:79%
to give it a try again and fly
this 747 simulator one more time.

01:21.445 --> 01:24.848 align:center line:79%
Before I had time
to fully process the question,

01:24.848 --> 01:31.788 align:center line:79%
I heard a voice sounding
astonishingly like my own, saying, “Yes,

01:31.955 --> 01:33.557 align:center line:81%
I would like that very much.”

01:35.459 --> 01:41.098 align:center line:79%
As soon as I said the words,
a tsunami of thoughts flooded my mind.

01:41.164 --> 01:45.636 align:center line:79%
It had been a long time since I
flew a 747. Back then, I was a young

01:45.669 --> 01:47.304 align:center line:81%
and confident captain.

01:48.071 --> 01:53.276 align:center line:79%
Now I had a reputation
to live up to as a former chief pilot.

01:54.344 --> 01:58.882 align:center line:79%
Would I embarrass myself
in front of these professionals?

01:58.882 --> 02:04.287 align:center line:79%
But it was too late to back down.
So I settled into the captain’s seat,

02:04.287 --> 02:07.157 align:center line:79%
placed my hands on the familiar
and beloved controls,

02:07.157 --> 02:11.962 align:center line:79%
and felt once again
the exhilaration of flight

02:12.362 --> 02:18.969 align:center line:79%
as the big jet roared down the runway
and took off into the wild blue yonder,

02:19.336 --> 02:22.005 align:center line:81%
even if it was only simulated.

02:23.840 --> 02:27.010 align:center line:79%
I'm happy to say
that the flight was successful.

02:27.010 --> 02:30.847 align:center line:79%
The aircraft remained intact,
and so did my self-image.

02:33.517 --> 02:38.121 align:center line:79%
Even so, the experience
was humbling for me.

02:39.189 --> 02:43.727 align:center line:79%
When I was in my prime,
flying had become almost second nature.

02:43.760 --> 02:48.865 align:center line:79%
Now it took all my concentration
to do the basic things.

02:49.766 --> 02:53.737 align:center line:79%
My experience in the flight
simulator was an important reminder

02:54.237 --> 02:59.743 align:center line:79%
that getting good at anything—
whether it be flying, rowing, sewing,

02:59.876 --> 03:06.683 align:center line:79%
or knowing—takes consistent
self-discipline and practice.

03:07.551 --> 03:11.988 align:center line:79%
You might spend years acquiring
a skill or developing a talent.

03:11.988 --> 03:14.991 align:center line:79%
You might work so hard that it
becomes second nature to you.

03:14.991 --> 03:20.964 align:center line:79%
But if you think that means you
can stop practicing and studying,

03:20.964 --> 03:26.403 align:center line:79%
you gradually lose the knowledge and
abilities you once acquired at great cost.

03:27.037 --> 03:31.341 align:center line:79%
This applies to skills like learning
a language, playing a musical instrument,

03:31.541 --> 03:33.009 align:center line:81%
and flying an airliner.

03:33.043 --> 03:39.683 align:center line:79%
It also applies to becoming
a disciple of Christ.

03:40.751 --> 03:41.785 align:center line:81%
Simply put,

03:43.153 --> 03:47.924 align:center line:81%
discipleship takes self-discipline.

03:49.025 --> 03:53.797 align:center line:79%
It is not a casual endeavor
and it doesn't happen by accident.

03:54.164 --> 04:01.371 align:center line:79%
Faith in Jesus Christ is a gift,
but receiving it is a conscious

04:01.671 --> 04:05.509 align:center line:81%
choice that requires a commitment

04:05.509 --> 04:08.278 align:center line:81%
of all our “might, mind and strength.”

04:08.278 --> 04:13.216 align:center line:81%
It is a practice of every day, every hour.

04:13.850 --> 04:16.953 align:center line:79%
It takes constant learning
and determined commitment.

04:17.387 --> 04:18.455 align:center line:81%
Our faith,

04:20.157 --> 04:22.959 align:center line:81%
which is our loyalty to the Savior,

04:23.894 --> 04:29.299 align:center line:79%
becomes stronger as it is tested
against the opposition we face here

04:29.299 --> 04:34.771 align:center line:79%
in mortality. It endures
because we keep nourishing it.

04:35.639 --> 04:38.909 align:center line:81%
We keep actively applying our faith,

04:40.410 --> 04:42.145 align:center line:81%
and we never give up.

04:42.979 --> 04:47.050 align:center line:81%
On the other hand, if we fail to use faith

04:48.118 --> 04:52.823 align:center line:79%
and its convincing
power by acting upon it,

04:53.490 --> 04:59.830 align:center line:79%
we become less sure of things we once
held sacred, less confident of

04:59.830 --> 05:01.965 align:center line:81%
things we once knew were true.

05:02.732 --> 05:06.536 align:center line:79%
Temptations that would never
have enticed us

05:07.771 --> 05:13.410 align:center line:79%
begin to look less
appalling and more appealing.

05:14.811 --> 05:20.517 align:center line:79%
The fire of yesterday's
testimony can warm us for only so long.

05:21.218 --> 05:25.555 align:center line:79%
It needs constant nourishment
to keep burning brightly.

05:26.289 --> 05:30.927 align:center line:79%
In the New Testament,
the Savior taught a parable about a master

05:31.995 --> 05:35.565 align:center line:79%
who gave each of his servants
a sacred trust,

05:35.565 --> 05:37.868 align:center line:81%
a quantity of money called “talents.”

05:38.735 --> 05:43.006 align:center line:79%
The servants who diligently
used their talents, increased them.

05:44.107 --> 05:49.212 align:center line:79%
The servant who buried
his talent eventually lost it.

05:50.080 --> 05:51.081 align:center line:81%
The lesson?

05:51.815 --> 05:56.553 align:center line:79%
God gives us gifts of knowledge,
of ability, of opportunity,

05:58.288 --> 06:04.461 align:center line:79%
and He wants us to use and amplify
them so they can bless us

06:04.461 --> 06:08.398 align:center line:81%
and bless God's other children.

06:09.499 --> 06:12.836 align:center line:79%
That doesn't happen if we put
those gifts high on a shelf,

06:12.836 --> 06:16.907 align:center line:79%
like a trophy that we admire
from time to time.

06:17.173 --> 06:24.214 align:center line:79%
Our gifts magnify and multiply only
when we put them to use—activate them.

06:25.382 --> 06:29.185 align:center line:79%
“But, Elder Uchtdorf,” you might say,
“I don’t have any gifts or talents.

06:29.185 --> 06:32.856 align:center line:81%
At least none are that valuable.”

06:33.823 --> 06:39.996 align:center line:79%
Well, perhaps you look at others
whose gifts are obvious and impressive,

06:39.996 --> 06:42.832 align:center line:79%
and you feel pretty
ordinary by comparison.

06:43.400 --> 06:46.169 align:center line:79%
You might suppose
that in the premortal existence,

06:46.169 --> 06:50.240 align:center line:79%
on the day of the great
gift and talent smorgasbord,

06:50.740 --> 06:53.410 align:center line:81%
your plate seemed woefully sparse,

06:54.577 --> 06:59.215 align:center line:79%
especially compared to the stacked
and overflowing plates of others.

07:00.650 --> 07:03.286 align:center line:81%
Oh, how I wish

07:04.454 --> 07:05.889 align:center line:81%
I could embrace you!

07:08.658 --> 07:09.659 align:center line:81%
And help you

07:10.827 --> 07:12.929 align:center line:81%
understand this great truth:

07:14.331 --> 07:22.238 align:center line:79%
You are a blessed being of light,
the spirit child of an infinite God.

07:23.006 --> 07:27.777 align:center line:79%
And you bear within
you a potential beyond

07:27.811 --> 07:31.081 align:center line:81%
your own capacity to imagine.

07:32.048 --> 07:37.420 align:center line:79%
As poets have noted, you come
to earth “trailing clouds of glory!”

07:38.822 --> 07:42.459 align:center line:81%
Your origin story is divine

07:43.960 --> 07:46.496 align:center line:81%
and so is your destiny.

07:47.697 --> 07:50.367 align:center line:81%
You left heaven to come here,

07:51.434 --> 07:54.437 align:center line:81%
but heaven has never left you.

07:56.506 --> 07:58.475 align:center line:81%
You are anything but ordinary.

07:58.508 --> 08:01.945 align:center line:79%
You are gifted! In the Doctrine
and Covenants, God declared,

08:02.245 --> 08:06.649 align:center line:79%
“There are many gifts, and to every
[person] is given a gift by the Spirit of

08:06.850 --> 08:09.819 align:center line:79%
God. To some is given one,
and to some is given another,

08:09.819 --> 08:12.589 align:center line:81%
and all may be profited thereby.”

08:13.023 --> 08:15.625 align:center line:79%
Some of our gifts are listed
in scriptures.

08:16.593 --> 08:18.661 align:center line:81%
Many are not.

08:20.397 --> 08:22.465 align:center line:81%
As the prophet Moroni said,

08:23.666 --> 08:29.472 align:center line:79%
“Deny not the gifts of God, for there are
many; and they come from the same God.”

08:31.041 --> 08:33.977 align:center line:79%
They might manifest themselves
in “different ways; ...

08:33.977 --> 08:38.681 align:center line:79%
but it is the same God
who worketh all in all.”

08:40.316 --> 08:43.987 align:center line:79%
It may be true that our spiritual
gifts are not always flashy,

08:45.488 --> 08:48.958 align:center line:79%
but that doesn’t mean
they are less important.

08:50.160 --> 08:54.564 align:center line:79%
May I share with you some spiritual
gifts that I have noticed in

08:54.564 --> 08:57.067 align:center line:81%
so many members across the world?

08:58.501 --> 09:03.973 align:center line:79%
Contemplate whether you have been blessed
with one or more gifts like:

09:05.708 --> 09:07.010 align:center line:81%
Showing compassion.

09:09.279 --> 09:12.782 align:center line:81%
Noticing people who are overlooked.

09:15.218 --> 09:18.655 align:center line:81%
Finding reasons to be joyful.

09:20.890 --> 09:22.625 align:center line:81%
Being a peacemaker.

09:24.360 --> 09:27.597 align:center line:81%
Noticing small miracles.

09:29.666 --> 09:32.268 align:center line:81%
Giving sincere compliments.

09:34.337 --> 09:35.338 align:center line:81%
Forgiving.

09:37.407 --> 09:38.408 align:center line:81%
Repenting.

09:40.143 --> 09:41.144 align:center line:81%
Enduring.

09:42.745 --> 09:44.380 align:center line:81%
Explaining things simply.

09:45.815 --> 09:47.450 align:center line:81%
Connecting with children.

09:48.852 --> 09:51.187 align:center line:81%
Sustaining Church leaders.

09:52.956 --> 09:56.392 align:center line:81%
Helping others know that they belong.

09:57.227 --> 10:00.563 align:center line:79%
You might not see these gifts
displayed at the ward talent show,

10:00.563 --> 10:05.602 align:center line:79%
but I hope you can see how
precious they are to the Lord's work

10:05.602 --> 10:10.140 align:center line:81%
and how you might have touched, blessed,

10:10.573 --> 10:15.678 align:center line:79%
or even saved one of God's
children by your gifts.

10:16.246 --> 10:22.085 align:center line:79%
Remember: “By small and simple
things are great things brought to pass.”

10:22.752 --> 10:27.991 align:center line:81%
So let us each do our little part.

10:29.959 --> 10:32.362 align:center line:79%
My beloved brothers
and sisters, dear friends,

10:32.362 --> 10:35.598 align:center line:79%
I pray that the Spirit
will help you recognize

10:36.833 --> 10:39.969 align:center line:81%
the gifts and talents God has given you.

10:40.403 --> 10:44.240 align:center line:79%
Then let us, like the faithful servants
in the Lord's parable,

10:44.240 --> 10:46.109 align:center line:81%
increase and magnify them.

10:46.876 --> 10:51.915 align:center line:79%
The day will come when we stand
before our compassionate Father in Heaven

10:52.615 --> 10:56.186 align:center line:81%
to give an account of our stewardship.

10:57.253 --> 11:01.391 align:center line:79%
He will want to know what we did
with the gifts He gave us, in particular,

11:01.391 --> 11:03.660 align:center line:81%
how we used them to bless His children.

11:04.060 --> 11:08.998 align:center line:79%
God knows who we truly are,
who we are designed to become,

11:09.599 --> 11:14.571 align:center line:81%
and so His expectations for us are high.

11:15.872 --> 11:20.476 align:center line:79%
But he doesn’t expect us
to take some grand, heroic,

11:21.010 --> 11:26.916 align:center line:79%
or superhuman leap to get there.
In the world He created,

11:27.951 --> 11:32.388 align:center line:81%
growth happens gradually and patiently,

11:32.822 --> 11:37.160 align:center line:81%
but also consistently and unrelentingly.

11:37.427 --> 11:39.596 align:center line:81%
Remember this: Jesus Christ ...

11:41.197 --> 11:48.571 align:center line:79%
Remember: It is Jesus Christ
who already did the superhuman part

11:49.839 --> 11:53.176 align:center line:81%
when He conquered death and sin.

11:54.244 --> 11:59.415 align:center line:81%
Our part is to follow the Christ.

12:00.750 --> 12:05.355 align:center line:79%
It is our part to turn away from sin,
turn toward the Savior,

12:06.189 --> 12:09.859 align:center line:81%
and walk in His way, one step at a time.

12:10.260 --> 12:13.630 align:center line:81%
As we do this diligently and faithfully

12:14.998 --> 12:17.133 align:center line:81%
with the desires of our hearts,

12:18.368 --> 12:22.772 align:center line:79%
we eventually cast off the shackles
of imperfections and faults

12:22.772 --> 12:27.610 align:center line:79%
and slowly become
refined until that perfect day

12:28.211 --> 12:31.514 align:center line:81%
when we will be perfected in Christ.

12:32.482 --> 12:34.117 align:center line:81%
The blessings are within reach.

12:34.317 --> 12:37.253 align:center line:79%
The promises are in place,
the doors wide open.

12:37.287 --> 12:41.591 align:center line:81%
It is our choice to enter and begin.

12:42.525 --> 12:45.328 align:center line:79%
The beginning may be small,
but that is okay.

12:47.597 --> 12:52.035 align:center line:79%
Where faith is weak,
begin with a hope in Christ Jesus

12:53.169 --> 12:57.940 align:center line:79%
and in His power to cleanse
and purify and reconcile

12:59.208 --> 13:02.745 align:center line:81%
and with a desire to follow Him.

13:03.713 --> 13:07.083 align:center line:79%
Our Father asks that we approach
this challenge of faith

13:07.083 --> 13:10.620 align:center line:81%
and discipleship not as a casual tourist,

13:12.088 --> 13:14.324 align:center line:81%
but as a wholehearted believers

13:15.458 --> 13:19.329 align:center line:79%
who leave behind an abandoned
Babylon and set their hearts, minds,

13:19.329 --> 13:21.431 align:center line:81%
and steps toward Zion.

13:23.032 --> 13:29.839 align:center line:79%
We know that our efforts alone
cannot make us celestial, but

13:30.940 --> 13:35.278 align:center line:79%
they can make us loyal
and committed to Jesus Christ,

13:35.578 --> 13:38.915 align:center line:81%
and He can make us celestial.

13:40.216 --> 13:42.251 align:center line:81%
Because of our beloved Savior,

13:42.251 --> 13:45.855 align:center line:79%
there is no such thing
as a no-win scenario.

13:46.589 --> 13:51.227 align:center line:79%
If we place our hope and faith in Him,
our victory is assured.

13:51.928 --> 13:57.467 align:center line:79%
He promises us access to His strength,
His power, His abundant grace.

13:57.734 --> 14:01.170 align:center line:81%
Step by step, little by little,

14:01.571 --> 14:05.508 align:center line:79%
we will grow ever closer
to that great and perfect day

14:05.908 --> 14:10.747 align:center line:79%
when we will live with Him
and our loved ones in eternal glory.

14:11.881 --> 14:15.718 align:center line:81%
To get there, we must do our part

14:15.785 --> 14:16.786 align:center line:81%
today

14:17.587 --> 14:18.688 align:center line:81%
and every day.

14:20.056 --> 14:23.659 align:center line:79%
We’re thankful for the steps
we took yesterday,

14:23.826 --> 14:25.261 align:center line:81%
but we don’t stop there.

14:25.695 --> 14:31.300 align:center line:79%
We know we still have a long way to go,
but we don't let that discourage us.

14:32.268 --> 14:34.704 align:center line:81%
That is the essence of who we are

14:35.838 --> 14:38.141 align:center line:81%
as followers of Christ.

14:39.409 --> 14:42.345 align:center line:79%
I urge and bless every member
of the Church and all

14:42.378 --> 14:44.247 align:center line:81%
who desire to be part of it

14:45.348 --> 14:48.785 align:center line:81%
to trust the Savior and engage patiently

14:48.785 --> 14:52.955 align:center line:79%
and diligently in doing your part
with all your heart,

14:54.123 --> 14:55.658 align:center line:81%
that your joy may be full,

14:55.658 --> 15:01.364 align:center line:79%
and that one day you
will receive all the Father has.

15:02.298 --> 15:04.033 align:center line:81%
Of this I bear witness

15:04.634 --> 15:07.837 align:center line:81%
in the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

